WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.300
Thank you for playing
"What's Behind Me?"

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.767
-That was so much fun.
-I appreciate that.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:06.000
It's the best.
-That was bizarre.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
-It is bizarre.
It's always great to see you.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.434
First of all,
congratulations on the

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:11.734
Independent Spirit Award
nomination.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:12.734
This is a giant.
-Thank you.

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:13.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:15.400
-Just now. Recently.
-Yeah.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.634
-That's major.
-Thank you.

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:18.334
Actually -- And I want to say
congratulations

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:20.868
to Marin Ireland,
one of my co-stars in "Eileen,"

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:22.300
and our director,
William Oldroyd,

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.267
because they got nominated, too.
-They got nominated, as well.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:28.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.167
-I know the film
was shot in New Jersey.

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.868
-Yes.
-And you are from New Jersey.

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:33.300
-Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.667
-You are a Jersey girl.
-Hello, hello. My queens.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:41.934
I have some facts that I don't
know if they're real or fake

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:45.601
that I got off the Internet
about you growing up,

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:46.901
and I just wanted to ask you
and maybe see --

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.000
-About me growing up
in New Jersey?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.868
-Yes. In New Jersey. Yes.
-Oh, my God!

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:51.901
-And see if any of these
are real or true --

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:54.167
-Oh, this is terrifying.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:55.834
-No. These are
all kind of interesting.

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:57.200
Okay.
-They're all good.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.868
-Okay.
-Here's one.

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:02.067
"Anne Hathaway once won a
free-throw shooting contest."

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:03.801
-[ Laughs ]
-Is this a true story?

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:07.634
-No. I mean, yes,
but I didn't win.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:08.767
-Okay.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.234
-So, it was
the Knights of Columbus...

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.100
-Yes! The Knights of
Columbus, yeah.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.968
-...sponsored
a free-throw competition

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:16.300
when I was 10, maybe.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:20.701
And I won the first round.

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:21.868
-You did?

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:23.801
-But then I choked
when we got to states,

00:01:23.801 --> 00:01:27.367
and so I did not win,
but I won a little bit.

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:29.734
-Were you athletic?
Are you athletic?

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:31.334
-I'm okay. I'm okay.

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:34.200
I -- When I was growing up,
I was really inconsistent.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.667
Like, I would, like,
have days where I was fire,

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.300
and then I would have days
where people would be like,

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.567
"Is it the same human?"

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:40.734
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.400
"She doesn't know
what she's doing at all."

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.634
How about this?

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:47.467
When you were 9,
you won your town's talent show.

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:50.234
-No. No. No, no, no.

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:53.701
It -- Well, first of all, it was
a Kiwanis Club talent show.

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:55.234
Clearly, we were big into clubs
growing up.

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:57.634
-Yeah. Wow. So Knights of
Columbus and Kiwanis Club.

00:01:57.634 --> 00:02:00.467
-Kiwanis Club. And they had --
It wasn't for my town.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.133
It was -- I don't know how --

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:04.534
what part of
New Jersey it was focusing on.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.801
And I didn't win,
but I did come in third.

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:09.734
-You didn't?
What was your talent?

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:11.400
-I don't know that you
would call it that,

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.801
but I sang a song called
"Johnny One Note,"

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.200
which is from --
which is a Judy Garland song.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.400
-"Johnny One Note"?
-"Johnny One Note."

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.767
But it was, like, crazy,
because the girl who won

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.200
was this classically
trained pianist,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.033
and she played this unbelievably
difficult sonata.

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:27.934
And then I went up there,
like, 9-year-old me,

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:31.367
and the downbeat hit
and the mic came up

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:33.434
and my left -- I remember this.

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:36.667
Right hand holding the mic.
Left hand just went...

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:40.434
And I stayed like that
the entire song.

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:43.734
But -- literally.
And it's a 3-1/2-minute song.

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:46.167
And just this. Just this.
So, yeah.

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:48.000
But I came in third.
-That's pretty good.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.634
It's wild. Yes.

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:52.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you very much. Thank you.

00:02:52.934 --> 00:02:54.200
-Did you have
a costume for this?

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.100
-I did. Oh my God, yes.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:59.400
I -- My mom
went to a thrift store,

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.634
and she got me
this little white bolero jacket.

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:04.467
A bolero jacket is one
that comes to here with this,

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:06.200
like, tiny, little collar.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.167
And then, guys,
she took red and black felt

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:11.534
and cut music notes...
-Come on.

00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:13.667
-...and glued them on and then
glued glitter on top of that.

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:15.467
-That's what I'm talking about
Mom. Come on!

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:17.734
-Mom. Absolutely.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:22.234
And then I wore the whole thing
on top. a shiny unitard.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:25.434
-Yeah, shiny unitard.
And only third place?

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:28.267
Come on! That's first place.
-Only third place.

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:30.000
-In our hearts.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.067
-I want to talk about "Eileen."
By the way, it's phenomenal.

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:36.033
-Thank you for watching it.
-Oh, I loved it.

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:39.133
-I love that you loved it.
I just -- I love it, too.

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:41.400
-Oh, it was great.
Also, you know what I love, too?

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.033
The -- Who plays Eileen.
Who is...

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:46.067
-Thomasin McKenzie.
She's incredible.

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:47.200
-I don't know her.
-Right?

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.200
-She's fantastic.
-I know her very well now.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.367
-Yeah. Now, yeah, sure.
-No, she's a joy.

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:56.267
And, like, we -- Like, this film
was super-duper intense, and --

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:58.234
-Oh, I didn't know
where it was going at all.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:03:59.934
-I know. I know.
-Set in the '60s.

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:01.267
-She's amazing.
She's a young actress.

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:04.934
She was in "Jojo Rabbit."
She was in "Old."

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:07.734
She's been in so many films.
"Power of the Dog."

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:09.200
And --
-You guys are great together.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.467
-She's incredible.

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:12.167
She's got a face like
it's carved from moondust.

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:15.133
She's so beautiful.
-Also, who directed this?

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:16.834
-William Oldroyd.
William Oldroyd.

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:19.934
And he directed
Florence Pugh's debut film,

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:21.334
which was called "Lady Macbeth."

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:22.901
-It's just so beautiful
to look at.

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:24.434
And the score is great,
by the way.

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:26.667
-Yes, Richard Reed Parry
from "Arcade Fire."

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:28.100
-No way!
-Yes.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.701
-Alright, this is all stuff
I didn't know, but I loved it.

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:33.834
And I go, "Okay, I kind of
understand where this is going,"

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:35.567
and then I was way off.
-Yeah.

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:36.834
-I did not know
where this was going.

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.767
-No.
-That last scene?

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:40.334
-Shh.
-No.

00:04:40.334 --> 00:04:42.567
Well, you'll see.
I won't say anything.

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:43.968
-I hope you go to see it.
-Yes.

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:45.701
-I really hope you
go to see it, because --

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:48.734
-How do we describe the film?
'60s.

00:04:48.734 --> 00:04:51.000
-It's a Christmas love story.
[ Laughs ]

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.501
-It is not. It is not
a Christmas love story.

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:54.133
-It's a Christmas love story,
Jimmy.

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:56.234
-No, that's not
how I would describe it.

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:59.734
-Every day on set, we would
be doing something so twisted,

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:02.667
and then Will would just go,
"It's a Christmas love story."

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:05.167
-Like, it is weirdly set
in the holidays.

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:07.534
-Yeah. But it is set 1964,
Christmastime,

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:11.100
Massachusetts, in the suburbs,
in one of those towns

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.667
with really
pretty picket fences,

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:13.834
but you don't know what's going
on inside anybody's home.

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:15.000
-Yeah.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.200
-And Thomasin McKenzie,
the wonderful girl

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.968
who I just -- a young actress
who I just described --

00:05:18.968 --> 00:05:23.367
she plays Eileen Dunlop,
who is a 24-year-old young woman

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:25.400
who works as a secretary
in a boys prison.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.801
-Yeah.

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:30.267
-And her life kind of seems like
it's over before it's begun.

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:33.367
And then...enter me.
-Enter you, yes.

00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:34.701
Of course. Yes.

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:37.267
-And I play
Dr. Rebecca St. John,

00:05:37.267 --> 00:05:39.968
who is a psychologist, and I've
come to the boys prison

00:05:39.968 --> 00:05:42.200
and I have some ideas of my own.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.000
-Yes. What a tricky role.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.767
And well-deserved
on that nomination.

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:46.801
-Thank you so much.

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:48.701
-I want to talk about --

00:05:48.701 --> 00:05:51.567
You have a scream
that is unbelievable.

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:52.901
-Yes, I do.
-Yeah.

00:05:52.901 --> 00:05:53.901
-You're showing the scream clip.

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:55.000
-Well, I'm going
to show the clip,

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.601
but, also, this --
IndieWire said that,

00:05:57.601 --> 00:06:01.467
"This is the year of
Anne Hathaway's primal scream,"

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:02.701
because you --

00:06:02.701 --> 00:06:04.601
-So, I can explain.

00:06:04.601 --> 00:06:08.734
I did a film
that came out earlier this year

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.067
in which I play a psychologist.

00:06:10.067 --> 00:06:11.367
I'm worried about
getting typecast.

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:13.000
-Yeah, typecast.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.934
-And she has a nervous breakdown

00:06:14.934 --> 00:06:16.634
and she screams
really loud in it.

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:20.067
And then, in this film,
there's a scream in it, as well.

00:06:20.067 --> 00:06:21.934
So, it's so, so weird
that you have two films

00:06:21.934 --> 00:06:23.534
that come out back-to-back
where you play psychologists

00:06:23.534 --> 00:06:25.033
who scream.

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:27.334
-Do you have -- I don't know
if I've ever heard you scream.

00:06:27.334 --> 00:06:28.968
I did in this film.
-Yeah.

00:06:28.968 --> 00:06:30.267
-But, I mean, wow!

00:06:30.267 --> 00:06:32.601
Are you used to --
Did you train to primal-scream?

00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:34.067
-To primal-scream?
-It is a primal scream.

00:06:34.067 --> 00:06:35.968
-I've been preparing
my whole life, Jimmy,

00:06:35.968 --> 00:06:37.234
to do a primal scream.

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:40.467
-I mean, it comes from your gut.
You're like, "Aaah!"

00:06:40.467 --> 00:06:42.968
I mean, it's like, wow!
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:44.467
-Does it feel good
to scream like that?

00:06:44.467 --> 00:06:47.734
-It feels fabulous.
It feels amazing, yeah.

00:06:47.734 --> 00:06:50.667
I just -- Yeah, I think --
Have you ever done it?

00:06:50.667 --> 00:06:54.000
-Uh, no. I think I bottled up
my primal scream.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.100
-Would you like to?
-I would -- I'd love to scream.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:58.968 --> 00:07:01.634
-I have a question.

00:07:01.634 --> 00:07:05.334
Has everybody
here made it through 2023?

00:07:05.334 --> 00:07:07.734
Did everybody make it
through 2022 before that,

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:09.968
2021 before that,
and 2020 before that?

00:07:09.968 --> 00:07:11.234
-Yeah.
-We're gonna primal-scream.

00:07:11.234 --> 00:07:12.934
Let's go. Come on.
-Oh, we're all going to do it?

00:07:12.934 --> 00:07:15.033
-We're all gonna do it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:16.834
Stand up.
-Oh, here we go.

00:07:16.834 --> 00:07:17.934
-Stand up. Hi.

00:07:17.934 --> 00:07:19.834
Taking control of the show.
I love it.

00:07:19.834 --> 00:07:21.734
-I'm excited to
scream with you today.

00:07:21.734 --> 00:07:22.801
So excited to stream with you.

00:07:22.801 --> 00:07:23.968
Is it okay that I
took control of the show?

00:07:23.968 --> 00:07:25.501
-I love that you took
control of my show, yes.

00:07:25.501 --> 00:07:27.334
Are you guys ready
to primal-scream?

00:07:27.334 --> 00:07:28.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:32.667
I mean, what is the tip?
What's a tips?

00:07:32.667 --> 00:07:34.868
-There is no trick.
Just let it out, guys.

00:07:34.868 --> 00:07:36.200
-Really?
-Okay? Ready?

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:39.801
-Primal scream. Here we go.
Here's to a great 2024.

00:07:39.801 --> 00:07:43.033
[ All screaming ]

00:07:43.033 --> 00:07:45.567
♪♪

00:07:55.701 --> 00:07:58.834
-Oh, my gosh. Wow! Let's go!

00:07:58.834 --> 00:08:00.868
-Whoo!
-It feels great!

00:08:00.868 --> 00:08:03.100
It feels great!
I want to show a clip.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:04.801
Here's Anne Hathaway
in "Eileen."

00:08:04.801 --> 00:08:06.434
Take a look at this.

00:08:06.434 --> 00:08:07.567
-You live here alone?

00:08:07.567 --> 00:08:10.133
-No. Oh, uh, sure.

00:08:10.133 --> 00:08:12.100
I, uh -- No,
I can't have roommates.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:15.334
I, um -- I like my own space,
I still like to have fun,

00:08:15.334 --> 00:08:17.934
and, uh, I can make
a lot of noise

00:08:17.934 --> 00:08:20.100
and, um, I can make a mess,
as you can see.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.734
But, uh, I can play music
as loud as I want to.

00:08:22.734 --> 00:08:26.634
I can -- I can scream
as loud as I want to.

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:28.033
[ Laughs ]

00:08:28.033 --> 00:08:29.801
[ Screams ]

00:08:29.801 --> 00:08:32.167
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:32.167 --> 00:08:34.567
-Come on!
-And now you know how to do it.

00:08:34.567 --> 00:08:37.133
-You're so good.
Watch this movie, everybody.

00:08:37.133 --> 00:08:40.133
It is fantastic.
"Eileen" is in theaters now.

